<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippines sees $100 mln in seaweed exports.</title>
<headline>Philippines sees $100 mln in seaweed exports.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-10-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines is projecting an additional $100 million every year in earnings after the European Parliament approved the export of Philippine seaweeds, trade and industry secretary Cesar Bautista said on Saturday.</p>
<p>The European Parliament approved on Thursday the classification of Philippine natural seaweed as a safe food additive.</p>
<p>&quot;The big size of the European market open for Philippine carrageenan (seaweeds) assures it of bigger export volumes and sales,&quot; Bautista said.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 Fax 8176267</p>
